    workbook=dict(
        question='Is our data ready, and what do we do in the next 90 days?',
        steps=['Build the inventory in the Information Inventory: at least six sources, each with an owner, a sensitivity label and a Ready for AI verdict.',
               'Rate the six areas Green, Amber or Red with one line of evidence each, read the total out of 12 and pick the top three gaps.',
               'Finish the AI Opportunity Portfolio (sheet People, risk, data): data readiness, a decision (Start now, Prepare first, Later, Drop) and one owner per entry; one entry to start now.',
               'Turn the gaps and the start-now entry into at least six roadmap lines with owner, dates, hours, what each waits for and a success measure.',
               'Put the day 30, 60 and 90 check-ins in the diary, list three risks to the plan and the decisions it needs, and write the day 90 target.'],
        fields=['My organisation and my plan start date', 'Sources in my inventory, and how many are Confidential or Personal', 'My six ratings, my total out of 12, my first Red',
                'My top three gaps, with evidence and a first fix', 'My final portfolio: the entry I start now, those I prepare first, those I drop',
                'My roadmap lines: action, owner, due date, hours, waits for, success measure', 'My sponsor and my data owners', 'Three risks to the plan and what I will do',
                'Decisions needed, who decides, by when', 'My check-in dates: day 30, day 60, day 90', 'My day 90 target: the score and one count', 'The action I take within 24 hours'],
        reflect=['Which area surprised me when I scored it?', 'Which portfolio entry did I drop, and why?', 'Which of the fifteen sessions changed how I think most?',
                 'What is AI, and where is it at work in my industry? My answer in two sentences.'],
        decision='How much my plan delivers by day 90 (one use finished, three gaps started, one folder tested, or data first), and my first action within 24 hours.'),
    facilitator=dict(
        prep=['Send the Follow-up Kit before the session if you can: 30-60-90 Check-in Form, Results Tracker, Sponsor Briefing (03 Learner Materials/Follow-up Kit). Check that each learner has editable copies of Information Inventory.xlsx, AI Opportunity Portfolio.xlsx and 90-Day Roadmap.xlsx, and their own portfolio from Sessions 0 to 13.',
              'Recorded run: demo_runs/s14/nvf_file_check.py (plain Python 3.12 with pandas, no AI model, 6 November 2026, one deterministic run). Output in nvf_file_check_output.txt: 60 invoice rows with 4 wrong totals, 2 missing PO numbers, 1 zero-VAT line and 1 invoice id shared by two rows (8 faults); 40 messages with 32 sender cells holding a phone number; 360 sales rows from 3 Aug to 19 Oct 2026 with no definition of revenue. All six counts on the six-checks slide come from this output. The script does not read the Busoga agreement or file dates: the two agreement copies (docx and txt, same text, nothing says which is signed) and the undated data files come from the Information Inventory grey example. Zero VAT (LL-2026-0464): the answer key says Lakeside Logistics charges 18% on its other invoices, so the line needs checking; do not say it breaks the law.',
              'Invented teaching values (fictional company, labelled on the slides): the five-row contact list (Carol blank, Brian twice); the NVF inventory rows, scorecard (6 of 12, Red on rights), portfolio (five entries, one Start now, three Prepare first, one Drop), roadmap (start 1 February 2027; check-ins 3 March, 2 April, 2 May 2027; 35 hours), and the day 90 target (9 of 12; invoice faults 8 to 0). They match the templates.',
              'Case sources and cautions (research/*.md): PUB-01 URA (URA 8 Apr 2025: a speech claim with no published method; ICTD paper 15 Jul 2019, may be out of date). ADO-03 Gartner (THE Journal 6 Aug 2024; a forecast, no later check found). ADO-07 GSMA (TelecomTV 16 Jul 2024; shares of identified uses, many are pilots). TEL-10 Vodacom (Google Cloud press release 25 Nov 2025; vendor announcement, no result). GAP-18 and GOV-05 National Data Strategy (Daily Monitor 21 Oct 2026; targets, not results; the AI strategy was not published as of 11 Nov 2026). MFG-05 BEES (Watchdog Uganda 24 Jun 2022; the source does not mention AI). Tour: BNK-02 KCB (The Star 7 May 2026; says data analytics and scoring, not AI), AGR-06 Dimitra and NACCU (AgNavigator 14 Oct 2025; an announcement with no result, and the article does not say which functions use AI. EU deforestation rule (EUDR): checked 12 Nov 2026, it applies from 30 December 2026 for large and medium operators and 30 June 2027 for micro and small ones (Regulation (EU) 2025/2650; EU Access2Markets). No further delay was proposed as of late October 2026. Re-check before teaching. Check the current status before teaching, and if asked, say the rule is why buyers want plot maps, whatever its date), HLT-04 Makerere AI Health Lab (Makerere CoCIS 2 May 2025; pilot).',
              'Agree each learner’s plan start date and how you will contact them before each check-in: message, email or call.'],
        demo_steps=['1. RECORDED: show the slide table; it is the saved output of the run of 6 November 2026. Say that no AI model is used: the script counts.',
                    '2. OPTIONAL LIVE (a few seconds, no internet): from the Build folder run python demo_runs/s14/nvf_file_check.py "../../03 Learner Materials/Practice Files/01 Case Company". The output must match nvf_file_check_output.txt.',
                    '3. Open customer_messages.csv: the sender column holds names with phone numbers, 32 of 40 rows. Ask which scorecard area this touches (Rights).',
                    '4. Open weekly_sales.csv and ask what revenue_ugx means: with VAT or without? The file does not say. That is a metadata gap.',
                    '5. Show the six-checks slide and the NVF scorecard; ask each learner to say aloud the first Red they expect in their own organisation.'],
        fallback='If the script cannot run, read nvf_file_check_output.txt and open the three CSV files in a spreadsheet to find one fault by eye. If the templates will not open, work on paper from the slide examples.',
        probes=[('Must we clean all our data before we start?', 'No. Start with one folder and one use. Fix the gaps that block that use, test it, then widen.'),
                ('Is 6 of 12 bad?', 'It is a starting point. A Red on rights matters more than the total: fix that first.'),
                ('Should we buy a data platform now?', 'Not before the inventory and the first test. Vodacom joined platforms at a scale of 223 million customers; most organisations get further first by fixing ownership, rights and copies. A platform needs its own business case, as in Session 11.'),
                ('Can we put personal data in an AI tool if we remove the names?', 'My understanding is that removing names may leave people identifiable through phone numbers or other details. Mask identifiers, test on invented samples first, and ask your lawyer what the 2019 Act requires.'),
                ('Who should own the roadmap?', 'One sponsor for the plan and one named owner for each line, with a deputy. A plan without owners does not move.'),
                ('What if nothing has started by day 30?', 'Say so at the check-in. Then choose one action, one owner and one date. A late start is normal; a silent plan is the risk.')],
        misconceptions=[('Data readiness is an IT job', 'IT runs the systems. Owners decide who may use each source, which is a leadership and legal decision.'),
                        ('The total score says whether we are ready', 'The total is a snapshot. A Red on rights stops the work whatever the total; the scorecard shows what to fix first.'),
                        ('AI will tell us what is wrong with our data', 'A plain script counted the NVF faults exactly. Count first; AI can help later.'),
                        ('More uses started means more progress', 'One use finished and tested at day 90 teaches more than five half started.')],
        questions=[('Name the six areas of the readiness scorecard.', 'Inventory, Readable, Complete and unique, Metadata, Rights, Current.'),
                   ('What are the four portfolio decisions?', 'Start now, Prepare first, Later, Drop, each with one owner.'),
                   ('What does every roadmap line need?', 'An action, one owner, a start and a due date, the hours, what it waits for, and a success measure someone else can check.')],
        rescue=['If a learner has no organisation to assess, use one team, one project or Nile Valley Foods with the supplied files.',
                'If the inventory runs long, stop at six sources and move on; the list can be finished after class.',
                'If the roadmap stalls, ask: which fix, if skipped, would make everything else unsafe? That is action 1.',
                'If time is short, do the check-ins block together during the close, using the slide picture.'],
        takeaway=['DATA READINESS, AI ROADMAP AND YOUR 90-DAY PLAN',
                  'Pilots stall on data: Gartner forecast (2024) that at least 30 in 100 generative AI projects would be dropped after the pilot, poor data quality named first.',
                  'Five kinds of data: tables (structured), text, images, audio, sensor data. First steps: define columns, find the current version, read the text and check a sample, transcribe and remove phone numbers, check for gaps.',
                  'Data inventory: every source with its owner, where it lives, who may see it, its sensitivity and whether it is ready for AI.',
                  'Check quality by counting (data quality dimensions): completeness, accuracy, consistency, timeliness, uniqueness, validity. Contact list: 4 of 5 phones filled; 4 different people in 5 rows.',
                  'Recorded run (6 Nov 2026, Python script, no AI model): NVF invoices 8 faults in 60 rows; 32 of 40 messages hold a phone number; sales revenue never defined.',
                  'Readiness scorecard: Inventory, Readable, Complete and unique, Metadata, Rights, Current. Green 2, Amber 1, Red 0, out of 12. NVF 6 of 12. A Red on rights stops the work.',
                  'Six steps: inventory, digitise, clean, describe, protect, test on 20 real questions. Start with one folder and one use.',
                  'Final portfolio: every entry with value, feasibility, people, risk, data readiness, a decision (Start now, Prepare first, Later, Drop) and one owner. Start one.',
                  '90-day plan: protect and clean (days 1 to 30), describe and prepare (31 to 60), test and decide (61 to 90). Every line: owner, due date, hours, what it waits for, a success measure someone else can check.',
                  'Check-ins: day 30 (controls in place? gap 1 closed?), day 60 (stop rule met? on time?), day 90 (score again; continue, expand, pause or stop).',
                  'Cases: URA register study (2019), Vodacom data platform first (2025), Uganda National Data Strategy 36% to 80% (2026), BEES at Nile Breweries (2022).',
                  'Within 24 hours: book the three dates and tell each owner their action. Follow-up Kit: Check-in Form, Results Tracker, Sponsor Briefing.'],
        one_learner=['Use the learner’s real organisation. If the learner leads a part of a larger company, assess one team, one folder or one use.',
                     '1. Recall (10 minutes): put the three questions, then ask what changed after Session 13.',
                     '2. Idea, cases and demonstration (30 minutes): teach as written; during the demonstration ask which of the learner’s files would give the worst count.',
                     '3. Inventory and scorecard (15 minutes): write the first three sources together, then let the learner continue. Ask for the evidence behind each colour; with none, the rating drops one step until checked.',
                     '4. Portfolio (15 minutes): go through each entry and ask why it starts now, waits or is dropped. Insist on one start-now entry.',
                     '5. Roadmap and check-ins (30 minutes): you play the sponsor. Ask what each line costs in hours, who covers when an owner is away, what would make the learner stop, and which decision is needed. Book the three check-in dates now.',
                     '6. People, decision and close (15 minutes): the learner names the sponsor and data owners, says the choice aloud, names a first action within 24 hours, then explains the fifteen-session picture in one minute and answers the Session 0 question in two sentences.'],
        group=['Pair learners by industry where possible. Each assesses their own organisation; the partner acts as sponsor.',
               'After the roadmap block, give each learner three minutes for their start-now entry, their first gap and its owner. The partner replies with one thing clear, one question and one risk.',
               'Ask the group which area was Red most often. That becomes the first topic at the day 30 check-in.',
               'Close by asking each learner to answer the Session 0 question in two sentences.']),
